From 81675aa1bc285ef42616aed9ca8bb334b2c1acf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:46:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Replace cockpit's PWM switch input with SRXL2, couple pilot
 head to rudder

cockpit_switch.c replaces the original Arduino sketch's pwm_input.cpp:
same 3-zone hysteresis classification (LOW/CENTER/HIGH) and the same
signal-loss fail-safe, but reading a channel MSRC already decodes out
of the SRXL2 stream (srxl2_channels.c) instead of measuring a PWM
pulse on a dedicated GPIO. Which channel is the switch, and which is
the rudder, are both single #defines in the new cockpit_channels.h
so they're easy to change later.

cockpit_task now carries the toggle behavior that consumed
pwm_input's zones in the original .ino, which this port hadn't had
at all until now: switching to HIGH toggles the pilot head's
movement on/off, switching to LOW toggles both displays (backlight)
on/off, CENTER itself does nothing, and losing the SRXL2 link forces
both back on as a fail-safe. Displays and head movement both start
off at boot; the Garmin bootscreen is shown once, the first time the
displays are switched on, never again after that, held non-blocking
via a timestamp instead of vTaskDelay so the servo/IMU keep updating
while it's shown.

piloten.c gains pilotenSetRudder()/a rudder bias (on top of the
existing roll bias, same architecture) and pilotenSetEnabled()/
pilotenGetEnabled() for the head-movement toggle, porting the
Enabled/parking logic from the newer single-servo piloten.cpp Ralph
sent along with the switch-channel and rudder-channel answers.

Channel numbers (switch = 5, rudder = 4) and the rudder bias sign
are reasonable defaults/assumptions - see the comments in
cockpit_channels.h and piloten.c's rudderBias() - flagged for
Ralph to confirm once hardware is in hand.
